\(\zeta (s)=1+\frac{1}{2^{s}}+\frac{1}{3^{s}}+\frac{1}{4^{s}}+\dots =\prod _{p\text{\ prime}}\frac{1}{1-p^{-s}}\)
Because every whole number is uniquely built by multiplying primes, the zeta function automatically encodes the DNA of every prime number inside it.

