When mathematicians write down the density of the Riemann zeta zeros (\(E_{n}\), where \(\zeta(\frac{1}{2} + iE_n) = 0\)), the fluctuating part looks virtually identical: [1] (https://arxiv.org/pdf/nlin/0212042)
\(d_{\text{Riemann}}(E)=-\frac{1}{\pi }\sum _{p\text{\ prime}}\sum _{k=1}^{\infty }\frac{\ln (p)}{p^{k/2}}\cos \big(kE\ln (p)\big)\)
Comparing the two equations side by side reveals a strict dictionary between chaos and prime numbers: [1] (https://empslocal.ex.ac.uk/people/staff/mrwatkin/zeta/GTF-RZF.htm), [2] (https://arxiv.org/pdf/nlin/0212042)

