The Standard Model Symmetry Group: \(SU(3)_C \times SU(2)_L \times U(1)_Y\)

Every elementary particle in the Standard Model is uniquely labeled by a triplet of irreducible representations—written as \((R_3, R_2, Y)\)—corresponding to the three fundamental forces (excluding gravity):
1. \(SU(3)_C\) (Strong Force / Color Charge):
