Modern quantum processors generalize Kitaev’s Toric Code in two major steps: first by flattening the donut onto a 2D planar chip (the Surface Code), and next by abandoning 2D nearest-neighbor geometry for high-dimensional expander graphs (qLDPC codes) to pack far more logical qubits into the same hardware.
